This change is wrong. By default, the HttpClient cache is a *private* cache (as it is a cache on the client-side) and so has different semantic than HttpCache (which is a reverse proxy cache).

Maybe those headers should be used in `isServerResponseCacheable` for the case where the cache is configured as a shared cache.
but they should not be added to the list of headers that always forbids caching in the RFC 9111 Section 3.1.

